{
    "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
    "annotation": "This workflow processes annotated Parse Bioscience single-cell RNA-seq data (.h5ad) from the Alzheimer's disease cerebral organoid Atlas: it aggressively filters cells at the beginning (set the threshold to suit your need, Galaxy resource limitations, etc..), then by doublet score, gene/UMI counts, mitochondrial percentage, and rare genes, then re-embeds the filtered data through scaling, PCA, neighborhood graph, UMAP, and Louvain clustering, producing QC violin/scatter plots, cluster marker genes, and final UMAP visualizations . It is adapted from a Scanpy 1.10.2 training pipeline to the Parse-specific obs/var keys (nCount_RNA, nFeature_RNA, percent.mt, doublet_scores, samples, leiden) and skips re-normalization since the input is already log-normalized. Input must contain obs: nCount_RNA, nFeature_RNA, percent.mt, doublet_scores, samples, leiden; var: gene_symbols, highly_variable, means. Workflow was created from a known-good Scanpy 1.10.2 workflow - https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/single-cell/tutorials/scrna-case_basic-pipeline/workflows/Filter-plot-and-explore-single-cell-RNA-seq-data-with-Scanpy.html",
